Subject: [PATCH] agent: republish operating channels after accepted renew

Controller startup deletes the persisted operating-class rows before
configuration renew. An already running agent has its initial channel-report
latch set, so it never republishes unchanged radios after that renew. A later
single-radio retune restores only that radio's current channel, leaving the
other bands absent from native inventory.

Rearm the existing all-radio publication after a renew is accepted. The
existing two-second tick waits for synchronized radios, reads their current
OneWifi channels and sends native operating-channel reports. Failed or busy
renew submissions do not rearm publication; normal operation remains one-shot.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/src/agent/em_agent.cpp
+++ b/src/agent/em_agent.cpp
@@ -457,6 +457,7 @@ void em_agent_t::handle_autoconfig_renew(em_bus_event_t *evt)
     }  else if ((num = static_cast<unsigned int>(m_data_model.analyze_autoconfig_renew(evt, pcmd))) == 0) {
         printf("handle_autoconfig_renew cmd creation failed\n");
     } else if (m_orch->submit_commands(pcmd, num) > 0) {
+        m_initial_op_channel_report_sent = false;
     }
 
 }
